  "statement": "Opus 5.5 High approves the reader-facing prose of the legacy briefs at this binding, which renders the byte-identical frozen content.json through the November 10, 2026 corpus amendment. Applied in memory, the amendment changes 259 of 46,254 corpus strings, only in link attributes: 40 Congressional Record hover labels and 269 links to the H.R.4405 engrossed bill text and H. Rept. 119-187. With title and href attributes removed, all 21 changed Markdown briefs are identical to dddc6ff, and no argument, response, evidence or link-text wording changed. All 48 brief pages re-render byte-identically from the amended corpus and pass verifyValue, and a second amendment pass changes nothing. Each corrected label repeats an existing corpus label and reads naturally where the prose names the maker: 'Representative Walberg quoted swimmer Riley Gaines' now cites Walberg's speech, the AFT clause cites the AFT letter, and 'the groups' letter' cites the National Women's Law Center and Women's Sports Foundation letter. I matched all 38 quotation-based corrections against the saved Record documents in docs/argument_key/evidence/*/manifest.tsv. Each quotation, split at ellipses and brackets, appears in the named maker's document and in no other maker's document for that bill and day. The two hand-attributed paraphrases (HR28_C11 scope and its procedure background copy) describe the letter they now cite. The recomputed publicationBinding equals legacy-binding.json.",
  "conditions": "Valid only for this exact binding (rendered-48b6275415aa183eebfc, content_sha256 654ead3c…) and the inherited issue identity. Install only together with the matching Sol 6.1 Max verification receipt for the same binding. Any change to content.json, the procedure, the mapping, any of the 29 rendered implementation files (including the four amendment files) or the issue source voids this receipt. publication.json must be updated separately to this binding and this receipt's hash; I did not edit it.",
  "limits": "Out of scope and not fixed: the label 'American Federation of Teachers; Randi Weingarten, President, AFT., letter inserted in the Congressional Record, June 9, 2026' (semicolon, title and doubled period) predates this amendment and comes from the source manifest's maker field; the amendment only applies it to one more H.R.5408 citation. Other issues the amendment does not change: different documents on one Record page still share one citation number (for example [1] for both the women's groups' letter and Walberg in HR28_C11, and [25] for Foxx and the AFT letter in HR5408_SEP_oppose_04); 16 H.R.5408 citations of CREC-2026-06-15-pt1-PgE573-3 keep a page-level label; some split evidence-note fragments inherit a whole note's Sources list. The amendment README names a build-amendment.mjs that is not in the repository; this does not affect rendering. With no network access, I did not reread GovInfo pages or check the replacement archive links; the maker checks used only the saved manifest documents, and the link replacements were checked only as attribute substitutions. The issue_release rendered_id (rendered-1aa1f935d40db7414f26) is the identity of the reviewed S.1582 issue artifact, carried forward as in earlier receipts. Its content, procedure and mapping IDs, issue_source and issue_version recompute unchanged, but a live identifyRenderedRelease now gives rendered-51607b8e817ffe315715 (rendered-57925cf16596a1a077f7 at dddc6ff), because the rendered-file list changed; no gate reads this field. I did not run the full publication gate, the build, the browser tests or the guided-review runtime checks covered by report-3.json, and I did not re-adjudicate the 101 inherited findings. No human comprehension or reliability test is claimed. Model and effort: claude-opus-5-5 per this session's system context, and high effort from the parent process command line, 'claude -p --model claude-opus-5-5 --effort high'.",
  "continuity": {
    "scope": "Citation-amendment continuity for the legacy briefs. Content, procedure and mapping are frozen and byte-identical. public-view.mjs now renders through the corpus amendment, rendered-release.mjs adds the four amendment files to the rendered binding, and the other 23 implementation hashes are unchanged.",
